reverts commit b9adeb2bbcbba2eb383a307bcfc756d32ebc43d7. ARC wake locks are now being handled in Chrome, so this API has no consumers.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:316686  Change-Id: I039baf7a2ee512f1d32a9cc55ea3483c2abd31f6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/315814 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="315814" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/system_api" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/system_api" ref="refs/changes/14/315814/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id3d9733fe3bdcf88ac82fb5a73d1b1d2296a1610" commit="1db2b873111c095850e76c32afb0a374484411f6" commit_message="[autotest] Add in teststation host class.  Add in the teststation host class to reduce the duplicated test station init code spread out among ADBHost and TestBed.  BUG=chromium:548739 TEST=Verified locally on moblab with moblab/angler and moblab/[beaglebone-dragon]  Change-Id: Id3d9733fe3bdcf88ac82fb5a73d1b1d2296a1610 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/314825 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="314825" owner_email="kevcheng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/25/314825/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I191e14303cdead164147d188ac495da6f7c18ba6" commit="4f1966c24597973d8d499f32856e2b1d98e8ce7b" commit_message="[autotest] test failure send email via a different gmail account  Test failures notification emails sometimes causing quota issues when a huge amount of notifications are sent out around the same time.  Move it to a different gmail account to gurantee that more critical emails like inventory emails can be sent out on time.  Also, add support for a &quot;creds&quot; dir.  TEST=send email using the new gmail account: - with gmail_api_credentials_test_failure and creds dir set.   confirm using new credentials. - without gmail_api_credentials_test_failure and creds dir set.   confirm using the default credentials. BUG=chromium:541824;chromium:567882  Change-Id: I191e14303cdead164147d188ac495da6f7c18ba6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316680 Commit-Ready: Fang Deng &lt;fdeng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Fang Deng &lt;fdeng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Fang Deng &lt;fdeng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="316680" owner_email="fdeng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/80/316680/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I88bc9a4c567a29556746d30e3febc37220db9f4b" commit="727a63bc9ef1ad2e7c9cffd3fb35c1d5af5f2f52" commit_message="Change linearity validator to test X vs Y  The linearity validator used to fit lines in X vs t and Y vs t (instead of X vs Y) which is more accurate, but requires a perfectly constant speed finger.  This is very difficult to do by hand, and basically requires a robot for a good test. We're trying to get Allion to perform more and more of our testing for us, but they don't have a robot right now, so this is likely causing false negatives.  This CL changes the linearity tests from the marginally more strict version to a slightly more relaxed version that works more accurately when done by hand.  BUG=chromium:567221 TEST=manually tested  Change-Id: I88bc9a4c567a29556746d30e3febc37220db9f4b Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316463 Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="316463" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" ref="refs/changes/63/316463/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I533a97a71bc32cbe8fa5c147dc5746c9a9016e8d" commit="0b06a15d89f2a7de35be0f9b223b4bac880174e6" commit_message="Quickstep gesture tweaks  This CL fixes a couple little issues with the Quickstep gesture  First: don't use the user entered speed when lowering the robot arm.  This can cause the robot's safety cutoffs to engage if you put in a high speed, since the robot thinks it's dropping to quickly. This changes it to drop slowly, then use the user entered speed once it's at the right Z height.  Second: I change the defaults to 60 speed and 30 passes which is what we've been using.  This way you don't have to specify  BUG=none TEST=manual  Change-Id: I533a97a71bc32cbe8fa5c147dc5746c9a9016e8d Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/315701 Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="315701" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" ref="refs/changes/01/315701/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6d764feaf933ad1694fb60fe2904d4e9d291ee10" commit="ddcdbf0329fd22dff577bcdb0f38e2b79ff9c8f0" commit_message="psmisc: remove from the whiltelist of building with clang.  BUG=chromium:504040 TEST=remove the workaround     CC=i686-pc-linux-gnu-clang