quot;  This reverts commit 3db7082585927a084399e847fe5fc50753ef6d54, which breaks several tests where DUT isn't pingable when configuring AP.  BUG=b/25129221 TEST=none  Change-Id: I3e0d746f2ba6ff6500f226bb3db5b9541cc0a676 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317010 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Roshan Pius &lt;rpius@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="317010" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/10/317010/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I65f11505912f17e778681fef8fcb567159e6ca4e" commit="49d649ddc7e79d37c23203c5fd1e8b00df3494f1" commit_message="ec-devutils: Add ec3po package to be installed.  The EC repo now contains a python utility called EC-3PO.  This commit allows that package to be installed when ec-devutils is.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46504 BRANCH=None TEST=sudo emerge ec-devutils; `python -c 'import ec3po'; print ec3po` in the chroot.  Verify that ec3po is installed in the site-packages.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:316701  Change-Id: I65f11505912f17e778681fef8fcb567159e6ca4e Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316437 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="316437" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/37/316437/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I59110e133d2af61db0230433d790717cf4e4ef05" commit="25c62e2ea359e0f674bf30106b6d5f87249c231e" commit_message="attestation: add preserve group  The attestation user needs to create files in /mnt/stateful_partition/unencrypted/preserve. To facilitate this we need a new group.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46244 TEST=manual  Change-Id: I59110e133d2af61db0230433d790717cf4e4ef05 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316070 Commit-Ready: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="316070" owner_email="dkrahn@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/70/316070/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icd76a799bae76024ec15abe860ad7aa44c8d45fa" commit="74a801f29f97858c674b26866c46bc36ce4c0356" commit_message="Add a 'preserve' group.  This group is intended to gate write access to /mnt/stateful_partition/unencrypted/preserve.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46244 TEST=manual  Change-Id: Icd76a799bae76024ec15abe860ad7aa44c8d45fa Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/315817 Commit-Ready: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="315817" owner_email="dkrahn@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/eclass-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/eclass-overlay" ref="refs/changes/17/315817/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4db224412ae3f5dfb045d99d90662a7c420cbcdb" commit="d739107c5cb618b2944b383ba03ba40eba8f33de" commit_message="devserver: Add locking around metadata read and write.  A race condition between reading and writing to the metadata file is causing update failures in the CQ.  Use a file lock to protect both reads and writes.  BUG=chromium:554773  Change-Id: I4db224412ae3f5dfb045d99d90662a7c420cbcdb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316913 Commit-Ready: Matthew Sartori &lt;msartori@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Matthew Sartori &lt;msartori@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="316913" owner_email="msartori@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/dev-util" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/dev-util" ref="refs/changes/13/316913/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1ea3fc9e567f53eaa81f9ae2470e6e02b83ad28e" commit="4fe9ab5a41fefd1bf33ca7e2177b62031102e374" commit_message="Read entire flash during verification when not paranoid  This makes verify_range() choose between two methods of verifying the ROM depending on the level of paranoia we're working under: 1. If we're paranoid, read and verify small chunks. This way we know    exactly where an error occurs and can handle it appropriately. 2. If we're not paranoid, read the entire ROM at once to reduce    transaction overhead.  The former approach is useful for Intel-based systems with a management engine (paranoid) where we may need to skip regions that are locked. The latter approach is designed to cut down on transaction overhead especially for external programmers.  On veyron_danger (4MB ROM), this resulted in a ~29 second speed-up when verifying the ROM content via Servo, from ~37s to ~8s. As expected, there was no significant difference when verifying using the &quot;internal&quot; SoC SPI controller.  Based on Simon Glass's patch to read entire flash at once during verification: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/#/c/240543/  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=Tested full and partial verify on veyron_danger and paine using &quot;internal&quot; programmers and Servo.  Signed-off-by: Simon Glass &lt;sjg@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I1ea3fc9e567f53eaa81f9ae2470e6e02b83ad28e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316007 Commit-Ready: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="316007" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/07/316007/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I77c487d68af4f58743672e5a8fa3a2a15c3d2b2e" commit="5c6345f0d775bb39236a7c2bfb472a5ebbde69f9" commit_message="Revert &quot;CHROMIUM: mmc: sdhci-tegra: Warn on register accesses while clock gated&quot;  This never caught any register accesses to the SDHCI with the clock disabled and is negatively affecting eMMC performance.  This reverts commit fa2b95ebd778416c50b916e22e504398cad2b93a.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48404 TEST=Build and boot on Smaug.  Change-Id: I77c487d68af4f58743672e5a8fa3a2a15c3d2b2e Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317320 Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317320" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/20/317320/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie30dcae83aa3f9eb0b97659c873a4eb5f83864e6" commit="ddc74ff1ec7ce3bae2c29620f1a5ca071e2140c1" commit_message="Add tests_policy_JavaScr